 "source_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ir3ATIsg0VM",
 "title": "Convergent vs Divergent Problem Solving",
 "topic": "mindset",
 "summary": "The creator explains the difference between convergent thinking, which assumes there is only one correct solution, and divergent thinking, which recognizes multiple correct solutions. He uses an example of a brick to show how divergent thinking opens up many possibilities for problem-solving in life.",
 "key_points": [
  "Convergent problem-solving has many variables and only one correct answer, which is what is typically taught in school.",
  "Divergent problem-solving means recognizing that there are many correct answers to a single problem.",
  "Most of life requires divergent solutions, not convergent ones.",
  "A person with a convergent process might only see a brick as something that builds a building.",
  "A person with a divergent process can see a brick as a doorstop, paperweight, gold spray-painted trophy, potted plant, or a walkway.",
  "People who struggle in life often only see one way out, treating every situation as a single brick wall in front of them."
 ],
 "content": "The creator discusses two types of problem-solving in life. The first type is convergent thinking, \"which is what they teach you at school, there's lots of variables and there's one correct answer.\" The second type is divergent thinking, \"which is that there's many correct answers to a single problem.\" The creator states that \"most of life is divergent solutions, not convergent solutions.\" He gives an example of a brick and asks, \"how many uses of a brick can you think of?\" Someone with a convergent process would only say \"bricks only build buildings.\" Someone with a divergent thinking process would think of multiple uses: \"as a doorstop, as a paperweight, spray paint it gold and make it a trophy, drill holes into it and use it as a potted plant... [and] for a pathway to walk on.\" The creator points out that \"there's so many different uses of a brick, but the people who struggle in life only see one way out and they see it as a brick wall in front of them.\"",
